  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_601f8ad960a04f2195c35dab22235db1",
      "statement": "AgentState is a TypedDict with three fields: messages (a reducer-based list of all conversation messages), jump_to (an ephemeral field for middleware to redirect execution), and structured_response (optional parsed structured output). Messages are accumulated via the add_messages reducer rather than replaced, preserving conversation history across iterations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L349-L355",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44503c793dd9f893d5ba0802082d28f5068e87be55e6e47ed7bf291c25e95709:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df5ae204b53d4496bcd30fa5206b8e80",
      "statement": "Agent execution uses ModelRequest to encapsulate model invocation inputs (model, messages, system_message, tools, response_format, state, runtime) and ModelResponse to return execution results (result messages list and optional structured_response). Middleware wrap_model_call handlers intercept ModelRequest before invocation and receive the handler callback for retries, short-circuiting, or modification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L272-L288",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:14f51ac777a0e4bd6d45fd8fd3d534dd9d72b54a6b2af8d7a71c68f3679ee2b2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L87-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea2a30a82990ea2528ae5aeb01f676bd28b1b645cbb046365933cb2ea32a0321:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88dd7b40c7054fadad9bdd9b648c3309",
      "statement": "ExtendedModelResponse allows middleware to return a ModelResponse paired with an optional Command for additional state updates. Commands are applied via graph reducers, so messages in commands are added alongside (not replacing) model response messages; non-reducer fields are overwritten by later commands.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L213-L261",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5404ae4a873489da2373636dee137a925338f578fb6fd654106ce9e3fbcc6aae:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L290-L313",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a9e5563aff24da8a5b4c4b3e197c89e7754e99898de5a58c40bf8ffa63dbcda3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_be098dc55d0a4a7b90cbe1d1069b324f",
      "statement": "Middleware execute at five lifecycle points: before_agent (once at start), before_model (before each model invocation), wrap_model_call (intercepts actual model call), after_model (after model invocation), and after_agent (once at end). Multiple middleware compose in registration order; wrap_model_call middleware are nested (first = outermost), while before_* and after_* hooks run sequentially.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L431-L501",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aa2dbf33279630d1cc44bd246b7c8765d6d98d5c4e289c0010ffeb0a6463989e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L503-L597",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4096b631cb7e5cc1f84308854075c32cfa0a013d05971ddb8ac3eef5b777521:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa90c1d9ff3242fc9f73397074872115",
      "statement": "Middleware before_model and after_model hooks can set state['jump_to'] to redirect execution to 'tools', 'model', or 'end'. The @hook_config(can_jump_to=[...]) decorator declares which destinations a hook is permitted to jump to, establishing conditional edges in the graph.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L523-L558",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:521fe2ea8752360085320e1befb75911a6f1329abdbb431c107b1302b189d882:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L879-L900",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:88672ca5fab7b88c4495126945ec71d455d1f00a74504f8a0fc6ca02cc4542d4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1ce1fcc293094ef8b859aa8e00de5326",
      "statement": "After model invocation, _make_model_to_tools_edge determines whether to dispatch tools or exit. It checks in order: explicit jump_to directive, presence of AIMessage, tool calls in AIMessage, pending (unexecuted and non-structured) tool calls, and whether structured_response has been populated. It returns Send commands for pending calls or destination strings for exit/loop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1923-L1975",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:964403b0cff43101e0a6d7fc69ae5b93dc942efb343cfc9f243a36cbe0684356:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28399de8706b4de9a4940d95163c6961",
      "statement": "_make_tools_to_model_edge decides after tool execution whether to continue the loop or exit. It exits if no AIMessage exists, if all executed client-side tools have return_direct=True, or if a structured output tool was executed. Otherwise it loops back to the model via loop_entry_node.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L2004-L2038",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4d2f05e92f40a9bf4105bce6ae4578bc49a8e2803c4a74c7e3f86cb5c8b91d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_054765800b1f4181ab92dd76273329fa",
      "statement": "When response_format is configured with ToolStrategy but no regular tools exist, _make_model_to_model_edge governs a loop where the model invokes structured output tools until a valid response is parsed. It checks jump_to, then structured_response presence, and loops back to model if neither condition is met.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1977-L2002",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78a3fe672d36eccea386e8f6e817ec5cdeccf57e50ce38238007004ee6655a47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_97e1308250d7487c879b74b73672b82e",
      "statement": "The ToolNode executes model-requested tools in parallel when possible. Tools are invoked via wrap_tool_call middleware handlers which receive ToolCallRequest (tool_call dict, BaseTool, state, runtime) and can retry, validate, cache, or skip execution by returning ToolMessage or Command.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1078-L1096",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:551cee9294f9305a3a7a7c9df2b9b8e501af2a288b6720d879c0f6e56a57b02c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L674-L755",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c3b22f27f7e6fc59e5c3c949b0f0d9c7f5b5ae8e0ba0541dfe43b06500b90c7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_622d8b0f4c3f4b32aefde7cf9ac99a7d",
      "statement": "When response_format uses ToolStrategy, synthetic tools are created for each schema. When invoked, the tool call arguments are parsed and validated; if valid, the parsed object goes to state['structured_response'] and the loop exits. If invalid and handle_errors is configured, a synthetic error ToolMessage is injected and the loop continues for model retry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1222-L1295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68cc95985ab4ccb254f448b23262b2deebd14679410afa69085074f4a8ebd50a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33c65dd1369546b5855d43024cc65c17",
      "statement": "Graph entry node is determined by middleware presence: before_agent if present, else before_model if present, else model. Loop entry (after tools) is before_model if present, else model. Loop exit (conditional edges source) is last after_model if present, else model. Exit node is last after_agent if present, else END. Middleware nodes chain in registration order.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1647-L1743",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5d4752fd45563b2294e6d0e37f5aff8f5ced6fd3f7b62a204f170a82d433a0b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6f03a00d76e84d2b9df99159d2c73d41",
      "statement": "The agent loop terminates when: (1) model does not call tools (tool_calls is empty), (2) middleware sets jump_to='end', (3) all pending tool calls are structured output tools, (4) a structured output tool is executed, (5) a tool with return_direct=True is executed, or (6) an unhandled exception occurs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1923-L1975",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:964403b0cff43101e0a6d7fc69ae5b93dc942efb343cfc9f243a36cbe0684356:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L2004-L2038",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4d2f05e92f40a9bf4105bce6ae4578bc49a8e2803c4a74c7e3f86cb5c8b91d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5fe06eae05cf4b75a168ebeb41435285",
      "statement": "Two strategies for structured output: ToolStrategy adds synthetic tools that the model invokes to provide structured data (works with any model, validates at parse time, slower). ProviderStrategy uses model-native structured output APIs (e.g., OpenAI's response_format, faster, provider-specific). AutoStrategy auto-detects at compile time based on model capabilities.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1347-L1440",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6e24d640bed15caf8ee74c3aa368f689e776daa29654e627127c1279f71ca1b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6af6572eef85470e9fd0c6c67a04f69a",
      "statement": "The messages field uses add_messages reducer, so returned Commands with {\"messages\": [msg]} append msg to the list rather than replace it. This preserves conversation history across iterations and ensures each model invocation has access to the full conversation and all tool results.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L237-L243",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90c2906591d5390e6dcbbc5e41b564f6f3d87e9476efdc5127ac996ebd3db382:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/middleware/types.py#L349-L355",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44503c793dd9f893d5ba0802082d28f5068e87be55e6e47ed7bf291c25e95709:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f38e06f65fc4c50b3a280406d6da207",
      "statement": "The agent graph is compiled with recursion_limit=9_999 to allow very long agent loops (hundreds of tool calls) while still protecting against infinite loops.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1829-L1835",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77c3c4c9a7eec5a3838f8f7fe0a5efba7f3a7cc85d27ef29572a4e8a0e4af9e6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0f2bbaa83f4a4dd9b9cff4cdeceeea21",
      "statement": "The model_node constructs a ModelRequest from current state, invokes wrap_model_call middleware if configured (passing _execute_model_sync as handler), and returns Commands that update messages and structured_response. Async variant amodel_node is provided for async-capable models.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1468-L1543",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54cd45424a6da345b6cdd58f06adae623405b4dd53cb45edf97323f1d2b57833:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_331e129b7a2847ea867de91e4906c897",
      "statement": "_chain_tool_call_wrappers composes multiple wrap_tool_call middleware into a single middleware stack where first-registered middleware is outermost. Each wrapper receives the request and a handler callback for the inner layers, enabling retry and interception patterns.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L658-L768",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f698f73bbdcf575280c38a0fafe57eb6ca684fa2347f96d8b7e425f9b415462:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bb8a178791b941109a2246cab91e4b8c",
      "statement": "_chain_model_call_handlers composes multiple wrap_model_call middleware into a single nested handler stack. Commands from each layer are accumulated in inner-first order and merged via _build_commands without merging individual commands.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L263-L352",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:272c0933c5414b8cecc2e64643c365fa65e76088a91d385cdab443f37076f035:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_15a9686f4ca24089a72a76df096e2c3a",
      "statement": "Agent state schema is resolved by merging state_schema (if provided by user) with middleware state_schema attributes. Later schemas override earlier ones when fields conflict. This allows middleware to extend state with custom fields while user-provided state_schema has highest priority.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1174-L1182",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79c59a206dc67c41cff7e2895b104673b0bf154adb4e716a7f0eb051aa756b95:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L452-L468",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:95231fc24c27b9e2345a191bbd3daa928421c5f14d8bdc0350fe29794a71adf1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ffd7448536a446eaa99cb79dc8171180",
      "statement": "_get_bound_model binds the model with tools and response_format configuration. It performs auto-detection of structured output strategy if needed, validates that middleware-added tools are registered or have wrap_tool_call handlers, and returns the bound model and effective response format.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1298-L1440",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a9262c2fd1ed4c970da50f7898b4bb2a19482839aef74c97348f9f14383141b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_92414361d4574c2283188893067eddef",
      "statement": "Model invocation exceptions propagate unless wrap_model_call middleware catches them. Tool execution exceptions propagate unless wrap_tool_call middleware catches them or ToolNode.handle_tool_errors is configured. Structured output validation errors can be configured to retry or raise via response_format.handle_errors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L628-L656",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00fd5f0b9df0762ae54ede2d60f5bbeb785b3055f04eeebf87c015e0171088de:"
        }
      ]
    }
